KZ2 patch 7003: getenv() looked up once on per-job, per-task, per-exit, per-file-op and per-FIFO-tick paths
(ps3recomp issue 243: the CRT getenv takes the environment lock and scans every variable on each call; a port on
Windows spent ~95% of two polling SPU threads there). New include/ps3emu/env_once.h: PS3_GETENV_ONCE("NAME") caches
the first result per expansion site. Applied to: spurs_job.c (SPURS_JOB_DESCDUMP, SPURS_JOB_DUMP, per job),
spu_lifted_job.h (SPURS_TASKSET_TRACE per task run, SPU_WORKER_TRACE per worker run; same change KZ3 is making
upstream), spu_workload.c (per job), spu_channels.c (YDKJ_CRI_EXIT_HALT / YDKJ_NO_CRI_R4 on stop and policy
entry), spu_dma.h, spu_interp.c, spu_raw.c, spu_coherency.c, spu_drain.c, ppu_fs.cpp (every file call),
cellGcmSys.c (per FIFO tick: GCM_CTXDBG, GCM_DRAINDBG), ppu_loader.cpp, ppu_sysprx.cpp. Behaviour is unchanged
when a variable is set at launch (nothing changes them later). Upstream: the toolkit-original sites go
via KZ3 (spurs_job, spu_lifted_job); the rest is a candidate on its own.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (hand-merged): cellGcmSys takes upstream (it already reads these once); ppu_fs keeps upstream with PS3_GETENV_ONCE substituted

(The spu_workload.c include hunk's context follows KZ3 patch 1136's include line.)
diff --git a/include/ps3emu/env_once.h b/include/ps3emu/env_once.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8cf38aa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/ps3emu/env_once.h
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+/* PS3_GETENV_ONCE("NAME"): getenv() looked up once per expansion site, then cached.
+ * Diagnostic and tuning gates on per-job, per-task or per-exit paths used to call getenv() every time; the
+ * CRT takes its environment lock and scans every variable on each call (ps3recomp issue 243: two polling SPU
+ * threads spent ~95% of their samples there on Windows, 14.1 fps against 29.8 once looked up once).
+ * Nothing in the runtime changes these variables after start-up. Racing first uses store the same pointer.
+ * GNU statement expression (gcc, clang, MinGW). */
+#ifndef PS3EMU_ENV_ONCE_H
+#define PS3EMU_ENV_ONCE_H
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#define PS3_GETENV_ONCE(name) __extension__ ({ \
+    static const char* volatile ps3_env_once_v_; static volatile int ps3_env_once_d_; \
+    if (!__atomic_load_n(&ps3_env_once_d_, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE)) { \
+        ps3_env_once_v_ = getenv(name); __atomic_store_n(&ps3_env_once_d_, 1, __ATOMIC_RELEASE); } \
+    ps3_env_once_v_; })
+#endif
